    "notes": "r* at the strict 0.5% bar is similar to the windowed operator (~1-8%), but the degradation curve above r* is dramatically better: at gate_frac=0.34, EMA produces Dppl=20.6% vs windowed w=256's 93.2% (4.5x improvement). The EMA cache also eliminates the second self_attn call entirely, making the per-gated-token cost O(D) instead of O(N*w). The value proposition is graceful degradation + real compute savings, not a higher strict r*."
